  "notes": [
    "Scheduling inputs, not measured promises for a new revision or a cold runner.",
    "Historical rows are [exact Cargo-domain signature, rounded-up Linux command seconds]. That serial run mixed warm and cold compilation.",
    "Observed rows are [domain, Linux seconds, Windows seconds, macOS seconds]. These are maxima of completed commands.json groups from the leaf, manifest and partial full runs; null means unmeasured, not zero.",
    "Target cache misses were observed for CLI defaults, CLI-v2 profiles, interactive, native-read, v2-run and workspace-read-v2. Native-read and CLI-v2-combined ran after another profile: a cache miss does not mean every command was cold.",
    "Headless Linux/Windows and leaf data-plane Linux/macOS include cache hits. macOS interactive/native-read/updater and most full Windows/macOS profiles remain unmeasured.",
    "Signatures bind program, isolated argv and test classification, not just profile names. Changed/new domains fall back to isolated scheduling.",
    "Full rows are [domain, rounded-up Linux command seconds, completed owned commands]. These full-only inputs come from command receipts at head 1402dd06497c8bb46e246ad3e5578fa84c6d68a2 in packed_full. All five sampled Linux profile jobs missed the target cache; dependencies hit, and compilation was reused within each job.",
    "Completed full rows exclude equivalent commands owned by another profile. They are lower bounds on a standalone cold domain, not complete cold-run promises; full packing retains per-domain floors, cold reserve and at most two domains.",
    "Incomplete full rows are censored prefixes, NOT duration estimates. Zero means the domain never started. These domains remain isolated with every original command retained.",
    "Groups 468264fc60318498 and 94b09b6fab6c103f exhausted 720-second executor budgets after respectively 21 and 17 successful profile commands. Full-profile packing now leaves additional execution headroom; affected weights are unchanged."
  ],
